{"account":{"geo":"iberia","title":"Iberia, 1100 BCE to now","author":"Jeremy Parra with Claude","extent":{"lon":[-11,6],"lat":[33.6,45.6]},"t_from":-1100,"t_to":2025,"cite":0,"note":"The first account; the toy began here."},"colonies":[{"tribe":"basque","keyframes":[[-1100,-0.9,43.1,270],[0,-1.1,43.0,240],[800,-1.7,43.0,180],[1500,-2.0,43.05,130],[1900,-2.2,43.1,95],[2025,-2.1,43.1,115]],"note":"The one pre-Roman tongue that never left. Once spoken on both sides of the Pyrenees (Aquitanian); squeezed, never replaced."},{"tribe":"iberian","keyframes":[[-900,-0.3,40.4,0],[-600,-0.3,40.4,280],[-200,-0.3,40.0,300],[0,-0.3,40.0,140],[100,-0.3,40.0,0]],"note":"Non-Indo-European tongues of the east and south coasts, written in their own scripts; gone under Latin by the first century."},{"tribe":"iberian","keyframes":[[-1100,-5.6,37.5,200],[-200,-5.6,37.5,220],[0,-5.6,37.5,90],[100,-5.6,37.5,0]]},{"tribe":"celtic","keyframes":[[-1100,-5.0,41.6,250],[-500,-5.0,41.4,350],[-100,-5.0,41.4,320],[50,-5.0,41.4,140],[200,-5.0,41.4,0]],"note":"Indo-European tongues of the meseta, the west and Gallaecia — and Gaulish to the north."},{"tribe":"celtic","keyframes":[[-1100,-8.0,42.5,180],[-100,-8.0,42.5,200],[100,-8.0,42.5,100],[250,-8.0,42.5,0]]},{"tribe":"celtic","keyframes":[[-1100,-7.3,39.4,150],[-150,-7.3,39.4,200],[50,-7.3,39.4,100],[200,-7.3,39.4,0]]},{"tribe":"celtic","keyframes":[[-1100,2.0,45.0,250],[0,2.0,45.0,200],[300,2.0,45.0,0]]},{"tribe":"punic","keyframes":[[-1100,-6.29,36.53,0],[-1000,-6.29,36.53,40],[-500,-6.29,36.53,70],[-237,-6.29,36.53,110],[-200,-6.29,36.53,60],[0,-6.29,36.53,20],[100,-6.29,36.53,0]],"note":"Traders' tongue of the coastal colonies — Gadir, Malaka, Ebusus, and Carthage's new city at Carthago Nova."},{"tribe":"punic","keyframes":[[-800,-4.42,36.72,0],[-750,-4.42,36.72,40],[-237,-4.42,36.72,80],[-100,-4.42,36.72,30],[50,-4.42,36.72,0]]},{"tribe":"punic","keyframes":[[-240,-0.98,37.6,0],[-227,-0.98,37.6,90],[-209,-0.98,37.6,60],[-100,-0.98,37.6,20],[0,-0.98,37.6,0]]},{"tribe":"punic","keyframes":[[-650,1.43,38.9,0],[-600,1.43,38.9,50],[-100,1.43,38.9,50],[100,1.43,38.9,0]]},{"tribe":"latin","keyframes":[[-218,1.25,41.1,0],[-150,-0.8,40.4,260],[-50,-3.0,40.2,400],[100,-4.0,40.2,520],[400,-4.0,40.2,560],[711,-4.0,40.4,540],[900,-4.0,40.6,0]],"note":"Carried in by legions and settlers from 218 BCE; by 400 it is everyone's tongue but the Basques'. It does not die — it splits."},{"tribe":"latin","keyframes":[[-206,-5.2,37.5,0],[-150,-5.2,37.5,200],[0,-5.2,37.5,250],[711,-5.2,37.5,250],[800,-5.2,37.5,0]]},{"tribe":"latin","keyframes":[[-120,0.5,44.4,0],[0,0.5,44.4,300],[500,0.5,44.4,300],[900,0.5,44.4,0]]},{"tribe":"mozarabic","keyframes":[[711,-4.6,37.8,0],[800,-4.6,37.8,320],[1000,-4.6,37.8,260],[1150,-4.6,37.8,120],[1250,-4.6,37.8,0]],"note":"The Latin-descended speech of al-Andalus — spoken by Christians, Muslims and Jews alike, written in Arabic or Hebrew letters; survives as refrains (kharjas) in Arabic poems."},{"tribe":"mozarabic","keyframes":[[711,-4.0,39.9,0],[800,-4.0,39.9,180],[1085,-4.0,39.9,200],[1200,-4.0,39.9,60],[1300,-4.0,39.9,0]]},{"tribe":"arabic","keyframes":[[711,-4.78,37.9,0],[720,-4.78,37.9,200],[950,-4.78,37.9,330],[1085,-4.78,37.9,330],[1236,-4.78,37.9,150],[1260,-4.78,37.9,0]],"note":"Arrives with a small elite in 711, becomes the language of learning and the street; recedes with the frontier but lingers as the Moriscos' algarabía until 1609 — and returns with migrants after 1990."},{"tribe":"arabic","keyframes":[[711,-3.6,37.0,0],[720,-3.6,37.0,120],[1238,-3.6,37.0,170],[1492,-3.6,37.0,170],[1502,-3.6,37.0,120],[1570,-3.6,37.0,60],[1610,-3.6,37.0,0]]},{"tribe":"arabic","keyframes":[[711,-0.5,39.0,0],[730,-0.5,39.0,150],[1238,-0.5,39.0,160],[1300,-0.5,39.0,140],[1500,-0.5,39.0,110],[1609,-0.5,39.0,90],[1612,-0.5,39.0,0]]},{"tribe":"arabic","keyframes":[[711,-4.0,39.9,0],[730,-4.0,39.9,170],[1085,-4.0,39.9,160],[1150,-4.0,39.9,60],[1250,-4.0,39.9,0]]},{"tribe":"arabic","keyframes":[[714,-0.88,41.65,0],[730,-0.88,41.65,150],[1118,-0.88,41.65,150],[1150,-0.88,41.65,50],[1200,-0.88,41.65,0]]},{"tribe":"arabic","keyframes":[[680,-4.5,34.4,0],[710,-4.5,34.4,230],[1200,-4.5,34.4,280],[2025,-4.5,34.4,300]]},{"tribe":"arabic","keyframes":[[1990,2.0,41.5,0],[2025,2.0,41.5,70,0.6]]},{"tribe":"arabic","keyframes":[[1990,-1.8,37.4,0],[2025,-1.8,37.4,80,0.6]]},{"tribe":"arabic","keyframes":[[2000,-3.7,40.4,0],[2025,-3.7,40.4,55,0.6]]},{"tribe":"berber","keyframes":[[-1100,-4.6,34.3,350],[1200,-4.6,34.3,330],[1900,-4.6,34.3,280],[2025,-4.6,34.3,250]],"note":"The Maghreb's own tongue — and the speech of most of the soldiers who crossed in 711, absorbed into Arabic and Romance within a few centuries."},{"tribe":"berber","keyframes":[[711,-4.5,38.8,0],[730,-4.5,38.8,200,0.7],[900,-4.5,38.8,120,0.6],[1050,-4.5,38.8,0]]},{"tribe":"castilian","keyframes":[[850,-3.7,42.8,0],[950,-3.7,42.8,100],[1037,-3.7,42.8,160],[2025,-3.7,42.8,180]],"note":"A frontier dialect from the hills north of Burgos that drove south like a wedge with the conquests, absorbed its neighbours, and crossed an ocean in 1492."},{"tribe":"castilian","keyframes":[[1050,-3.8,40.4,0],[1100,-3.8,40.4,220],[1300,-3.8,40.3,330],[1600,-3.8,40.3,380],[1900,-3.8,40.3,420],[2025,-3.8,40.3,460]]},{"tribe":"castilian","keyframes":[[1225,-4.8,37.7,0],[1260,-4.8,37.7,200],[1492,-4.8,37.7,300],[2025,-4.8,37.7,330]]},{"tribe":"castilian","keyframes":[[1240,-2.6,37.6,0],[1270,-2.6,37.6,170],[1492,-2.6,37.6,250],[2025,-2.6,37.6,290]]},{"tribe":"castilian","keyframes":[[1000,-4.6,42.0,0],[1100,-4.6,42.0,190],[2025,-4.6,42.0,250]]},{"tribe":"galport","keyframes":[[850,-8.2,42.3,0],[950,-8.2,42.3,160],[2025,-8.2,42.3,180]],"note":"From the northwest, south down the Atlantic coast with the Portuguese conquests to the Algarve by 1249 — then to Brazil."},{"tribe":"galport","keyframes":[[1100,-8.3,39.6,0],[1150,-8.3,39.8,170],[1250,-8.2,39.4,260],[2025,-8.2,39.4,280]]},{"tribe":"catalan","keyframes":[[850,1.8,42.0,0],[950,1.8,42.0,130],[1150,1.6,41.8,170],[2025,1.6,41.8,180]],"note":"From the Frankish march around Barcelona to Valencia and the islands with the Crown of Aragon in the 1230s; a sea-tongue across the Mediterranean."},{"tribe":"catalan","keyframes":[[1238,-0.4,39.2,0],[1260,-0.4,39.2,120],[2025,-0.4,39.2,140]]},{"tribe":"catalan","keyframes":[[1229,2.9,39.6,0],[1240,2.9,39.6,90],[2025,2.9,39.6,90]]},{"tribe":"leonese","keyframes":[[850,-6.0,42.8,0],[950,-6.0,42.8,150],[1230,-6.0,42.8,170],[1500,-6.0,42.9,120],[1900,-6.0,43.0,70],[2025,-6.0,43.1,55]],"note":"The Romance of the old Asturian kingdom; outranked by Castilian from 1230 and retreating to villages ever since."},{"tribe":"aragonese","keyframes":[[850,-0.8,42.3,0],[950,-0.8,42.3,110],[1150,-0.9,42.0,170],[1500,-0.6,42.4,110],[1700,-0.4,42.6,60],[2025,-0.3,42.65,35]],"note":"Spoken along the Ebro and the Pyrenean valleys; now held on to in a few high valleys."},{"tribe":"ladino","keyframes":[[1492,-5.37,35.57,0],[1500,-5.37,35.57,50],[1950,-5.37,35.57,50],[1975,-5.37,35.57,0]],"note":"The Castilian of 1492, carried out by expelled Jews and kept for centuries — in Thessaloniki until 1943, in Istanbul and northern Morocco still."},{"tribe":"occitan","keyframes":[[850,0.6,44.3,0],[950,0.6,44.3,260],[1539,0.6,44.3,260],[1900,0.6,44.2,190],[2025,0.6,44.1,90]],"note":"Context north of the Pyrenees — the troubadours' tongue, pushed back by French from 1539."},{"tribe":"french","keyframes":[[1539,1.0,46.2,0],[1700,1.0,45.8,200],[1900,1.0,45.2,330],[2025,1.0,44.9,380]],"note":"Context: the state language arriving from the north."},{"tribe":"native","keyframes":[[-1100,-4.0,40.2,600],[-200,-4.0,40.2,600],[0,-4.0,40.2,450,0.8],[200,-4.0,40.2,260,0.6],[400,-4.0,40.2,80,0.4],[500,-4.0,40.2,0]],"note":"Local gods of springs, mountains and warriors — Endovelicus, Ataecina, Lugus. Overlaid by Rome, then slowly replaced."},{"tribe":"native","keyframes":[[-1100,-1.8,43.0,120],[600,-1.8,43.0,100,0.7],[1000,-1.8,43.0,0]]},{"tribe":"native","keyframes":[[-1100,-4.6,34.3,350],[700,-4.6,34.3,300,0.6],[800,-4.6,34.3,0]]},{"tribe":"phoenician","keyframes":[[-1100,-6.29,36.53,0],[-1000,-6.29,36.53,50],[-237,-6.29,36.53,110],[0,-6.29,36.53,50],[200,-6.29,36.53,0]],"note":"Melqart's temple at Gadir — later Hercules Gaditanus — Tanit and Baal Hammon in the colonies."},{"tribe":"phoenician","keyframes":[[-800,-4.42,36.72,0],[-750,-4.42,36.72,40],[-237,-4.42,36.72,70],[0,-4.42,36.72,0]]},{"tribe":"phoenician","keyframes":[[-240,-0.98,37.6,0],[-227,-0.98,37.6,80],[-150,-0.98,37.6,30],[0,-0.98,37.6,0]]},{"tribe":"phoenician","keyframes":[[-650,1.43,38.9,0],[-600,1.43,38.9,50],[100,1.43,38.9,0]]},{"tribe":"greek","keyframes":[[-600,3.12,42.13,0],[-550,3.12,42.13,45],[-50,3.12,42.13,45],[50,3.12,42.13,0]],"note":"Artemis and Asclepius at the Greek trading town of Emporion — a small, long-lived foothold."},{"tribe":"greek","keyframes":[[-600,5.37,43.3,0],[-580,5.37,43.3,60],[-50,5.37,43.3,60],[100,5.37,43.3,0]]},{"tribe":"roman","keyframes":[[-206,-2.0,39.0,0],[-100,-3.0,39.5,300],[0,-4.0,40.2,500],[250,-4.0,40.2,520],[380,-4.0,40.2,220,0.6],[420,-4.0,40.2,0]],"note":"Jupiter, the Capitoline triad, and the worship of the emperor — the public religion of the cities."},{"tribe":"roman","keyframes":[[-120,0.8,44.3,0],[0,0.8,44.3,280],[380,0.8,44.3,200],[420,0.8,44.3,0]]},{"tribe":"judaism","keyframes":[[50,1.25,41.12,0],[150,1.25,41.12,35],[600,1.25,41.12,30],[700,1.25,41.12,15],[1000,1.25,41.12,20]],"note":"An urban network, never a territory: Roman-era communities, a golden age in Córdoba, Lucena and Granada, the aljamas of the Christian kingdoms, the pogroms of 1391, expulsion in 1492 — and a diaspora that carried Iberia out with it."},{"tribe":"judaism","keyframes":[[50,-6.34,38.92,0],[150,-6.34,38.92,35],[612,-6.34,38.92,30],[700,-6.34,38.92,15],[900,-6.34,38.92,0]]},{"tribe":"judaism","keyframes":[[300,-4.02,39.86,0],[400,-4.02,39.86,40],[612,-4.02,39.86,35],[700,-4.02,39.86,20],[900,-4.02,39.86,50],[1300,-4.02,39.86,60],[1391,-4.02,39.86,55],[1420,-4.02,39.86,30],[1492,-4.02,39.86,30],[1493,-4.02,39.86,0]]},{"tribe":"judaism","keyframes":[[700,-4.78,37.88,0],[800,-4.78,37.88,55],[1000,-4.78,37.88,75],[1148,-4.78,37.88,60],[1170,-4.78,37.88,0]]},{"tribe":"judaism","keyframes":[[800,-4.48,37.41,0],[900,-4.48,37.41,45],[1100,-4.48,37.41,55],[1148,-4.48,37.41,0]]},{"tribe":"judaism","keyframes":[[800,-3.6,37.18,0],[900,-3.6,37.18,40],[1066,-3.6,37.18,55],[1090,-3.6,37.18,20],[1492,-3.6,37.18,15],[1493,-3.6,37.18,0]]},{"tribe":"judaism","keyframes":[[900,-0.88,41.65,0],[1000,-0.88,41.65,45],[1391,-0.88,41.65,45],[1420,-0.88,41.65,25],[1492,-0.88,41.65,25],[1493,-0.88,41.65,0]]},{"tribe":"judaism","keyframes":[[900,2.5,41.7,0],[1000,2.5,41.7,50],[1391,2.5,41.7,50],[1400,2.5,41.7,15],[1492,2.5,41.7,15],[1493,2.5,41.7,0]]},{"tribe":"judaism","keyframes":[[1248,-5.98,37.39,0],[1260,-5.98,37.39,50],[1391,-5.98,37.39,50],[1400,-5.98,37.39,15],[1492,-5.98,37.39,15],[1493,-5.98,37.39,0]]},{"tribe":"judaism","keyframes":[[1150,-9.14,38.72,0],[1200,-9.14,38.72,40],[1492,-8.6,39.6,120],[1496,-8.6,39.6,120],[1498,-8.6,39.6,0]]},{"tribe":"judaism","keyframes":[[1492,-5.37,35.57,0],[1500,-5.37,35.57,50],[1950,-5.37,35.57,45],[1975,-5.37,35.57,0]]},{"tribe":"judaism","keyframes":[[1960,-3.7,40.42,0],[1980,-3.7,40.42,20],[2025,-3.7,40.42,25]]},{"tribe":"judaism","keyframes":[[1960,2.17,41.39,0],[1980,2.17,41.39,20],[2025,2.17,41.39,25]]},{"tribe":"converso","keyframes":[[1391,-5.0,38.6,0],[1420,-5.0,38.6,170,0.7],[1480,-5.0,38.6,170,0.7],[1600,-5.0,38.6,120,0.4],[1700,-5.0,38.6,0]],"note":"Jews baptised under pressure after 1391 and by force in Portugal in 1497 — watched by the Inquisition, some keeping Jewish practice in secret. Many 'Portuguese' families fled to Amsterdam and became Jews again. Spinoza's was one of them."},{"tribe":"converso","keyframes":[[1497,-8.3,40.0,0],[1500,-8.3,40.0,170],[1650,-8.3,40.0,140,0.7],[1800,-7.5,40.4,50,0.5],[2025,-7.35,40.36,15,0.4]]},{"tribe":"arian","keyfr